      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Our Story",
        "heading": "13 years of building more than bikes",
        "story_text": "<p>In 2012, James and Ian opened a small workshop in Hackney with one goal: prove that anyone can build a bicycle frame.<\/p><p>Today, we use bamboo bicycle building for prison rehabilitation, school programmes, and community projects. Every bike we help create connects people — to craft, to purpose, and to each other.<\/p>",
        "founder_quote": "If we want people to choose sustainable options, we need to offer something better than what polluting products can be.",
        "founder_name": "James Marr",
        "founder_role": "Founder",
        "timeline_title": "Key Milestones",
        "visual_position": "right",
        "content_width": "60-40",
        "vertical_align": "top",
        "mobile_order": "text_first",
        "gap_size": "lg",
